The network uplink is healthy; the failure is in name resolution. From host_1_1_1_1, all data center IPs are reachable (e.g., ping 10.200.0.3/.4/.5/.6 succeeds, and default gateway 10.1.1.1 responds). However, host_1_1_1_1 is configured to use 10.200.0.2 as DNS (resolv.conf), and DNS lookups are being refused. An nslookup/dig from host_1_1_1_1 to 10.200.0.2 returns status REFUSED with “recursion requested but not available.” On dns_server, BIND is running and listening on 10.200.0.2:53, but /etc/bind/named.conf explicitly sets “recursion no;” and there are no internal zones defined (named.conf.local is empty). As a result, the DNS server is neither authoritative for your internal hostnames (e.g., web_server_0) no
